  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1011 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nOverall, it looks like the Fall-like weather will largely continue \nthrough Friday. A stout upper ridge will build over the central CONUS\nand into the South this next week as an upper trough persists over \nthe eastern seaboard. By Thursday/Friday, the upper ridge starts to \npush eastward as a shortwave trough swings over the north-central \nportion of the country. Meanwhile, surface high pressure looks to \nremain entrenched over the Great Lakes and down into the Deep South \nthrough the week. Overall, little to no rainfall will be the theme \nthrough this next work week. Highs warm into the 70s for much of the \nweek before increasing into the lower 80 degrees for some locations \nby late week as the axis of the aforementioned upper ridge moves over\nthe the region. Lows will generally remain in the 40s for most of \nthe week. Although, some locations may see lows around 50 degrees by \nThursday night. Ultimately, it might be a good idea to grab at least \na light jacket when heading out the door this week!",
